<subpara id="X39400000R4015C_10" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___00002PS00000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The throttle position sensor is mounted on the throttle body, and converts the throttle valve opening angle into a linear voltage signal of approximately 0 to 5V, which it outputs to the engine control computer. The output system is 2-fold redundant to improve the reliability of the detection section.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A084577J04" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</item>
</list1>
